  "summary": "Michael Johnson Jr. is a Sports Administration student at the University of Cincinnati, pursuing a Bachelor of Science in Sports Administration with an expected graduation in 2027. He is building a strong academic and professional foundation in athletic operations, event management, and organizational leadership. He is also completing professional certificate coursework from Cornell University in Labor Relations and Business Contracts, strengthening his understanding of the business side of athletics.\n\nHe will be interning with the University of Wisconsin–Madison Athletics Department, where he will gain hands-on experience in the business and operational side of Division I athletics. In this role, he will support daily operations, assist with game day and special events, and collaborate with staff to understand logistics, planning, coordination, and the internal processes that drive a successful athletic program.\n\nIn addition, he serves as a Summer Youth Baseball Coach and Summer Sports Coordinator for the Black Men Coalition Youth Baseball Program, where he oversees program logistics while mentoring young athletes. He emphasizes discipline, accountability, and personal development while ensuring smooth program execution.\n\nHe has also volunteered with the Boys & Girls Club during summer months, supporting efforts to provide meals to children and families in need while assisting with community outreach initiatives.\n\nMichael has further experience working on a mayoral campaign in Chicago, where he supported outreach efforts, coordinated logistics, assisted with event planning, and helped organize community engagement activities. This role strengthened his ability to operate in fast-paced, detail-oriented environments requiring strong communication, scheduling, and execution skills.\n\nHis experience also includes event staffing with organizations such as ProCamps and the Boys & Girls Club of Dane County, where he supported large-scale events, managed logistics, and engaged with diverse audiences to ensure successful execution.\n\nAcross his experiences, he has developed skills in event operations, program coordination, leadership, communication, and community engagement. He is continuing to build toward a career in athletic administration and sports operations, with a focus on the business and organizational aspects that drive success in the sports industry.",
